    "title": "Pedestrian fatally struck in south St. Louis: SLMPD - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Daesha Gear ,\n1 hours ago ST. LOUIS – The St. Louis Metropolitan Police Department (SLMPD) is investigating a deadly hit-and-run that happened in the Gravois Park neighborhood Wednesday evening.\nAccording to SLMPD, investigators from Accident Reconstruction were alerted to a pedestrian crash at Winnebago and Ohio around 7:20 p.m.\nPolice say one person was fatally struck by a vehicle. Officials say the suspected vehicle involved in the fatal crash left the scene.\nSLMPD is urging drivers to avoid the area.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX 2.",
